WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.447
A missing pivot cell should not automatically be changed to zero.

00:00:04.447 --> 00:00:10.032
Zero can mean that the observation exists and its measured value is zero.

00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:14.498
A null value can mean that there was no recorded observation at all.

00:00:15.154 --> 00:00:20.828
For example, zero monthly sales may mean we know the product had no sales.

00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:25.558
A null value may mean we have no record for that product and month.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:30.769
Those are different facts, and later averages or models may treat them differently.
